    <data name="More_Options_ButtonTooltip.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>More options</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_PrivacyNotice.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Good to know</value>
    <comment>Title of the note behind the (i) button: facts about where snippets expand and how undo works</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_PrivacyNotice_Expansion.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Snippets don't expand in apps running as administrator or in standard Windows password boxes. They can still expand in password fields on websites and in some apps.</value>
    <comment>First bullet of the "Good to know" note</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_PrivacyNotice_Undo.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Right after a snippet expands, Ctrl+Z changes it back to what you typed, except for snippets that use your clipboard or ask you to type something.</value>
    <comment>Second bullet of the "Good to know" note. Snippets that "ask you to type something" are the ones with {{prompt:…}}.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_PrivacyNotice_SensitiveInfo.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Don't save passwords, Social Security numbers, credit card numbers or other sensitive info in snippets. They're saved as plain text and aren't encrypted.</value>
    <comment>Privacy warning, the first bullet of the "Good to know" note. You may replace "Social Security numbers" with the national ID number people use in your market</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_PrivacyNotice_InputMethod.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If you type with an input method editor (IME), for example for Japanese, Chinese or Korean, switch it to direct input or English before you type a trigger.</value>
    <comment>Third bullet of the "Good to know" note. An input method editor turns keystrokes into characters, as for Japanese, Chinese or Korean; use the name Windows uses in your language</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_GoodToKnowButton.[using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Automation]AutomationProperties.Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Good to know</value>
    <comment>Screen reader name of the button that opens the "Good to know" note; the same as the note's title</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_GoodToKnowButton.[using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Good to know</value>
    <comment>Tooltip of the button that opens the "Good to know" note; the same as the note's title</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_ElevatedEditingNotice.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can't edit snippets while PowerToys runs as administrator</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_ElevatedEditingNotice.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To edit snippets, restart PowerToys without administrator rights. If Always run as administrator is on in General, turn it off first.</value>
    <comment>"Always run as administrator" is the name of a setting on the General page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_ElevatedSnippetAccessDenied" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Restart PowerToys without administrator rights to edit snippets.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SyncHeading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use your snippets on all your PCs</value>
    <comment>Bold heading of the sync advice in the snippets database menu, while the snippets database isn't inside OneDrive. Two numbered steps follow it. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SyncStepMove" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Select {0} and save it in OneDrive or another synced folder.</value>
    <comment>Step 1 under "Use your snippets on all your PCs". {0} is the name of the "Move snippets database…" button, shown bold. "It" is the snippets database. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets. OneDrive is a product name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SyncStepUse" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On each of your other PCs, select {0} and pick that database.</value>
    <comment>Step 2 under "Use your snippets on all your PCs". {0} is the name of the "Sync from another PC…" button, shown bold. "That database" is the snippets database saved in step 1. "Snippets database" (or "database") means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SyncHeadingOneDrive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use these snippets on your other PCs</value>
    <comment>Bold heading of the sync advice in the snippets database menu, while the snippets database is inside OneDrive. One sentence follows it. Text Expander only compares the database's path with the OneDrive folder; it doesn't check the sync itself. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SyncStepOneDrive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On each PC, select {0} and pick this database.</value>
    <comment>Follows "Use these snippets on your other PCs". {0} is the name of the "Sync from another PC…" button, shown bold. "This database" is the snippets database in use, in OneDrive. "Snippets database" (or "database") means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryDefault" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved on this PC · {0} snippets</value>
    <comment>{0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryDefault_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved on this PC · {0} snippet</value>
    <comment>{0} is the number 1.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryDefaultCountUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved on this PC</value>
    <comment>Shown when the snippets database can't be read, so there is no count. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryCustom" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved in {1} · {0} snippets</value>
    <comment>{0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. {1} is the name of the folder the snippets database is in, such as Documents. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryCustom_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved in {1} · {0} snippet</value>
    <comment>{0} is the number 1. {1} is the name of the folder the snippets database is in, such as Documents. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryCustomCountUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved in {0}</value>
    <comment>{0} is the name of the folder the snippets database is in, such as Documents. On the button that opens the snippets database menu, and shown when the database can't be read, so there is no count. "Snippets database" (or "database") means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryOneDrive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved in OneDrive · {0} snippets</value>
    <comment>The snippets database is inside OneDrive. OneDrive is a product name. {0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryOneDrive_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved in OneDrive · {0} snippet</value>
    <comment>The snippets database is inside OneDrive. OneDrive is a product name. {0} is the number 1. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryOneDriveCountUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved in OneDrive</value>
    <comment>The snippets database is inside OneDrive. OneDrive is a product name. On the button that opens the snippets database menu, and shown when the database can't be read, so there is no count. "Snippets database" (or "database") means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SummaryElevated" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not available while PowerToys runs as administrator</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_Move.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Move snippets database…</value>
    <comment>Button: opens the Windows Save dialog to choose a new place for the snippets database, such as a folder OneDrive syncs. Text Expander writes the snippets there and uses that database; the previous one stays where it was. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_Use.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sync from another PC…</value>
    <comment>Button: opens the Windows Open dialog to choose an existing snippets database, such as the one another PC saved in OneDrive. Text Expander uses that database from then on and writes nothing. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_OpenButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open in text editor</value>
    <comment>Button in the snippets database menu: opens the snippets database in the app Windows uses for JSON files, or in Notepad when no app is set for them. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets. JSON is a file format name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_OpenMissing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The snippets database can't be found or accessed. Select Refresh, or choose it again.</value>
    <comment>"Refresh" is the button beside Open in text editor. "It" is the snippets database. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_OpenFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Windows couldn't open the snippets database. Check that a default app is available for JSON files, then try again.</value>
    <comment>Shown when Open in text editor can't open the snippets database, a .json file, in the app Windows uses for JSON files, or in Notepad when no app is set for them. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets. JSON is a file format name and is not translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_OpenSnippetsErrorDialog_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can't open the snippets database</value>
    <comment>Title of the dialog shown when Open in text editor fails. The reason follows it. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_ReloadButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Refresh</value>
    <comment>Button in the snippets database menu: reads the snippets database again. The same in every state; it doesn't sync anything itself. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_ReloadButton.[using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls]ToolTipService.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Read the snippets database again. Text Expander also does this automatically when the database changes.</value>
    <comment>Tooltip of the Refresh button. "Snippets database" (or "database") means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_Conflict_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This database already has snippets</value>
    <comment>Title of the dialog shown when Move snippets database… picked a snippets database that already has snippets, after Windows asked to replace it. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_Conflict_Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use the snippets in {0}, or replace them with this PC's snippets. Text Expander backs up the database before replacing it.</value>
    <comment>{0} is the snippets database's file name, such as PowerToysTextExpanderSnippets.json. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_Conflict_Use" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use its snippets</value>
    <comment>Button: uses the database's own snippets instead, and writes nothing, as Sync from another PC… does. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_Conflict_Replace" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Replace them</value>
    <comment>Button: backs up the database, then writes this PC's snippets over it. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_Reloaded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Snippets refreshed.</value>
    <comment>Status after the user selected Refresh and the snippets database was read again. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_WaitingForFile" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your snippets database isn't there right now, so the list stays as it is. It's read again when the file is back, and saving a snippet writes it again.</value>
    <comment>Status after the user selected Refresh while the snippets database was missing, for example for a moment while another app saves it. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SavedDefault" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your {0} snippets are now saved on this PC.</value>
    <comment>Status after Move snippets database… wrote them to a snippets database in the folder on this PC that Text Expander uses by default. {0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SavedDefault_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your {0} snippet is now saved on this PC.</value>
    <comment>Status after Move snippets database… wrote it to a snippets database in the folder on this PC that Text Expander uses by default. {0} is the number 1. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SavedOneDrive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your {0} snippets are now saved in OneDrive.</value>
    <comment>Status after Move snippets database… wrote them to a snippets database inside OneDrive. OneDrive is a product name. {0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SavedOneDrive_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your {0} snippet is now saved in OneDrive.</value>
    <comment>Status after Move snippets database… wrote it to a snippets database inside OneDrive. OneDrive is a product name. {0} is the number 1. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SavedCustom" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your {0} snippets are now saved in {1}.</value>
    <comment>Status after Move snippets database… wrote them to a snippets database. {0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. {1} is the name of the database's folder, such as Documents. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_SavedCustom_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your {0} snippet is now saved in {1}.</value>
    <comment>Status after Move snippets database… wrote it to a snippets database. {0} is the number 1. {1} is the name of the database's folder, such as Documents. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_ReplacedBackedUp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The database you replaced was backed up.</value>
    <comment>Follows "Your … snippets are now saved in …" when Move snippets database… replaced a snippets database, which it backed up first, beside itself. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_UsingDefault" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Now using the {0} snippets on this PC.</value>
    <comment>Status after Sync from another PC… switched to a snippets database in the folder on this PC that Text Expander uses by default. {0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_UsingDefault_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Now using the {0} snippet on this PC.</value>
    <comment>Status after Sync from another PC… switched to a snippets database in the folder on this PC that Text Expander uses by default. {0} is the number 1. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_UsingOneDrive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Now using the {0} snippets in OneDrive.</value>
    <comment>Status after Sync from another PC… switched to a snippets database inside OneDrive. OneDrive is a product name. {0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_UsingOneDrive_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Now using the {0} snippet in OneDrive.</value>
    <comment>Status after Sync from another PC… switched to a snippets database inside OneDrive. OneDrive is a product name. {0} is the number 1. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_UsingCustom" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Now using the {0} snippets in {1}.</value>
    <comment>Status after Sync from another PC… switched to a snippets database. {0} is the number of snippets, two or more, or zero. {1} is the name of the database's folder, such as Documents. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_UsingCustom_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Now using the {0} snippet in {1}.</value>
    <comment>Status after Sync from another PC… switched to a snippets database. {0} is the number 1. {1} is the name of the database's folder, such as Documents. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_NotSnippets" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} doesn't look like a snippets database</value>
    <comment>Title of a dialog with no other text, shown when Sync from another PC… picked a file that isn't a snippets database: not JSON, or without a list of snippets. Text Expander didn't switch to it. {0} is the file's name, such as settings.json. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets. No period: it's a title.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_FileType" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Snippets database (*.json)</value>
    <comment>File type in the Save and Open dialogs of Move snippets database… and Sync from another PC…. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets. Keep "(*.json)", the file name pattern; JSON is a file format name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFile_ChooseDifferent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose a different database</value>
    <comment>Default button of the "… doesn't look like a snippets database" dialog: opens the Windows Open dialog again. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_Error_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Couldn't update the snippets database</value>
    <comment>Title of the dialog shown when Move snippets database… or Sync from another PC… fails. The reason follows it. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_SettingsSaveFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>PowerToys couldn't save the new snippets database setting, so Text Expander still uses the database it used before.</value>
    <comment>Shown when switching to another snippets database fails because the PowerToys setting that stores its location couldn't be saved. Nothing changed. "Snippets database" (or "database") means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_SettingsCommittedAfterError" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>PowerToys saved the new snippets database setting, but couldn't finish the settings update cleanly. The new database is in use. Check the settings file at {0}, and keep these recovery files until you have verified it: {1}.</value>
    <comment>{0} is the full path to settings.json. {1} is a semicolon-separated list of settings recovery files, or the settings path when no separate recovery file exists. "Snippets database" (or "database") means the user's JSON file of snippets. The settings file and recovery files are PowerToys settings files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetFolder_SettingsStateUncertain" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>PowerToys couldn't verify which snippets database setting is stored. No snippets databases were removed. Restart PowerToys, check the settings file at {0}, and keep these recovery files until the snippets database in use is confirmed: {1}.</value>
    <comment>{0} is the full path to settings.json. {1} is a semicolon-separated list of settings recovery files. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets. The settings file and recovery files are PowerToys settings files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_Dialog_Cancel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cancel</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_Dialog_Close" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Close</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_Row_CaseInsensitiveAutomation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Case-insensitive trigger: {0} or {1}</value>
    <comment>{0} is the lowercase trigger and {1} is the uppercase trigger.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_Row_Inserts" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>inserts</value>
    <comment>In the snippet list, between a snippet's trigger and the text it inserts, like "maps to" in Keyboard Manager. Lowercase, as it follows the trigger</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_Row_AsksThenInserts" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>asks {0} then inserts</value>
    <comment>In the snippet list, between the trigger of a snippet that asks questions and the text it inserts. {0} is the questions, each shown as a bubble. Lowercase, as it follows the trigger</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_AddSnippetButton.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>New snippet</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_NoSnippets.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No snippets yet</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_CantOpen" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can't open your snippets</value>
    <comment>Title of the error shown when the snippets database can't be read or saved, or isn't a snippets database. The reason follows it. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_NotJson" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your snippets database has a mistake on line {0}. Fix it in a text editor, then select Retry.</value>
    <comment>Follows "Can't open your snippets" when the snippets database isn't valid JSON, for example after a hand edit. {0} is the line number where the mistake was found. Text Expander doesn't save over it. "Retry" is the button next to this message. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_NoList" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your snippets database is missing its "snippets" list. Fix it in a text editor, then select Retry.</value>
    <comment>Follows "Can't open your snippets" when the snippets database is JSON but has no list named "snippets". "snippets" in quotes is the name used in the file and is not translated. Text Expander doesn't save over it. "Retry" is the button next to this message. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_CantFind" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can't find your snippets database</value>
    <comment>Title of the error shown when the snippets database the user chose isn't where it was. Text Expander doesn't create a new one there. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_CantFindHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>It was moved, renamed or deleted. Put it back and select Retry, or choose it again.</value>
    <comment>Follows "Can't find your snippets database", with its path. "It" is the snippets database. "Retry" is the button next to this message, and "Sync from another PC…" follows it. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_CantReachOneDrive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can't reach your snippets in OneDrive</value>
    <comment>Title of the error shown when the snippets database inside OneDrive can't be reached, for example because OneDrive isn't running. OneDrive is a product name. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_CantReachOneDriveHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check that OneDrive is running and you're signed in, then select Retry. To keep working now, choose another database.</value>
    <comment>Follows "Can't reach your snippets in OneDrive". OneDrive is a product name. "Retry" is the button next to this message, and "Sync from another PC…" follows it. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_CantReachCustom" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can't reach your snippets in {0}</value>
    <comment>Title of the error shown when the snippets database's folder can't be reached, for example because it was deleted or its drive isn't connected. {0} is the name of the folder, such as Documents. "Snippets database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_SnippetError_CantReachCustomHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check that the drive or network folder is available, then select Retry. To keep working now, choose another database.</value>
    <comment>Follows "Can't reach your snippets in {0}". "Retry" is the button next to this message, and "Sync from another PC…" follows it. "Database" means the user's JSON file of snippets.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_EditSnippet.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Edit</value>
    <comment>First item in a snippet's More options menu; opens the snippet in the editor</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="TextExpander_DuplicateSnippet.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Duplicate</value>
  </data>
